[Fm]Man, revealing [Ab/Eb]God [Fm]to [Db]man.

Verse 3:
[Fm]God yet [Db]speaks [Cm]by [Fm]His own [Eb/G]Spirit
[Fm]Speaking [Db]to [Cm]the [Fm]hearts [Eb/G]of [C/E]men,
[Bbm]In the [Fm]age-long [Db]Word [Cm]expounding
[Bbm]God's [Cm]own [Fm]message, [Db]now [Cm]as [Fm]then;
[Ab]Through [Eb/G]the [C/E]rise [Fm]and [Bbm]fall [Fm]of [Ab/C]nations
[Ab]One [Eb/G]sure [C/E]faith [Bbm]yet [Cm]standing [Ab/C]fast,
[Fm]God is [Cm]King, [Fm]His [Ab/Eb]Word [Db]unchanging,
